Z||000000||firstfiero||05-07-2001||08:37 AM||||    This morning when I turned on my defroster a smoke came out of the vents and it smelled like anti freeze. Is this my heating core going bad? I don't know if it's because of this but my sub woofer just ****  the bed also. Making a loud thumping sound. anything I should know about installing a fiero heating core?<P>------------------<BR>Hey Mr. Ricer come over here and tell me how your stickers make you faster.....<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/headshot.gif">         <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Ken Wittlief||05-07-2001||09:46 AM||||For a temp fix get a 90° bend plastic pipe from the 'Help' race at the autoparts store, or a 1/2" piece of copper pipe, and pull the hoses off the front firewall and bypass the heatercore.<P>  thats what I did this weekend till i get around to replaceing the core - cost me 20 cents for the short piece of copper pipe. (the hoses are 1/2" inside diameter to the heatcore, so you need a 1/2" outside diameter pipe, about 2 to 3" long.<P>  Also if you have a wet vac the floor on the passengers side of the car is probally wet with antifreeze. Take the seat out and hose it out good, that stuff never seems to evapporate on its own.||||reg||1
Z||000002||84Bill||05-07-2001||03:40 PM||||Yeah she be toast good thing it didnt go when rolling down a highway off ramp like it did on my wifes subaru. Winshield went from perfect to total fog in about 1/10th of a second ||||reg||9
Z||000003||TOM||05-07-2001||05:46 PM||||The heater cores are very easy to replace on an AC car. two hoses under the hood. And four screws under the dash to remove the cover. Oh yes and the sub box.||||reg||1
